## Critical: `write-mode=REMOTE_ONLY` ≠ Catalog SoT

Current `REMOTE_ONLY` = **strict sync mirror**: remote fail aborts request, but **web-backend still owns the write** (local row is primary until Wave 7 proxy CRUD).

| Mode | Who owns the card write |
|---|---|
| `enabled=false` / `LOCAL_ONLY` | web-backend only |
| `DUAL` | web-backend primary; catalog best-effort after commit |
| `REMOTE_ONLY` (today) | web-backend still writes; catalog must succeed in-request |
| Wave 7 cutover | **catalog-service primary**; local mirror or read-only, then drop |

## Wave 6 exit criteria (ops, not green unit tests alone)

1. `catalog_db` + `catalog-service` up; health OK  
2. Backfill categories → products  
3. `GET /products/catalog-service/verify` → `countsMatch=true`, sample missing = 0  
4. Outbox: no stuck FAILED; retry works; Kafka (if on) no silent loss  
5. Soak on `DUAL` ≥ agreed window without upsert/error storm  
6. Exercise `read-mode=REMOTE_ONLY` + failover (catalog down → expected behavior)  
7. Offline cashier: offline ≥1 day, multi-update, deactivate, reconnect, duplicate/out-of-order snapshots idempotent  
8. Only then decide Wave 7 write-cutover

## Staging soak (ship path)

Compose: `docker-compose.prod.yml` + `docker-compose.staging.yml` — services `catalog-db` / `catalog-service` included.  
Safe default: `CATALOG_SERVICE_ENABLED=false`.

1. Set in staging `.env`: `CATALOG_DB_PASSWORD`, `CATALOG_INTERNAL_API_KEY`  
2. `docker compose -f docker-compose.prod.yml -f docker-compose.staging.yml up -d --build catalog-db catalog-service`  
3. Health: `curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:18090/api/v1/actuator/health`  
4. Flip `CATALOG_SERVICE_ENABLED=true`, `WRITE_MODE=DUAL`, recreate backend  
5. `POST …/products/catalog-service/backfill-categories` then `…/backfill/all`  
6. `GET …/verify` → `countsMatch` + `sampleMissingRemote=0`  
7. Soak DUAL; watch `…/status` outboxFailed=0  
8. Do **not** enable write REMOTE_ONLY / drop `products` until Wave 7

